; claude: the teletype's programs, as Talk.talk values
; (plan_terminal.md): the games of David Ahl's "101 BASIC Computer
; Games" and their kind, so that one program runs alone (a thin main,
; examples/TeletypeHangman.ml) and under TinyTerminal's shell
; (apps/system/), a command each. Tty_hangman, Tty_guess, Tty_wumpus.
;
; Over libs/terminal's Talk, no Playground: the Teletype way is what
; puts them on a screen (its programs have no model, no update, no
; view). In the package tiny_appkits, as tiny_appkits.appkit_teletype,
; pure OCaml, so every backend can run them.
(library
 (name appkit_teletype)
 (public_name tiny_appkits.appkit_teletype)
 (wrapped false)
 (libraries terminal) ; Talk
)
